00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.290
Let's go, Imber!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:15:00.370
Honki misechau yo, kanaechau kara
I'll show you for real, because I'll make it come true

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:04.620
Sora o tsukinuketa sekai de
In a world that's pierced through the skies

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:11.830
Fushigi na omoi kanjita yo, shunkan de suki!
I felt a strange emotion, I liked you in an instant!

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:09.120
Is that were Haruka and the others are?

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:11.040
That is correct.

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:14.200
You have my apologies. I-

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.580
Egao de katsu desho
I'm sure I'll win with a smile

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:15.950
It was inevitable.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:19.950
Yappa egao wa tadashii no
Sure enough a smile is the right way

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:20.450
After all, Haruka is the "first penguin".

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:25.500
Naiteta chiisa na watashi ga tachimukau
I was small and crying but I'll rise to the challenge

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:22.370
The first...?

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:28.330
It refers to the first penguin in the flock
that leaps into the dangerous ocean.

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.700
Nandaro doki doki
I wonder what this palpitation is

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:31.000
Chotto teate ga hitsuyou ne
I need a little medical attention

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:31.040
It is used to describe a courageous person.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:39.160
Binetsu na kibun wa anata no sei kamo, S.O.S!
This feeling of slight fever could
be your fault, S.O.S!

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:53.540
But doesn't it just make
you reckless to leap

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:56.580
without considering the consequences?

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.040
Upperclassman...

00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:59.250
Yeah, but...

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.950
...it sounds just like them.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:05.080
Yes, it describes them perfectly.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.080
So that's... Aulyn!

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.290
We've finally made it this far.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.160
Yeah!

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:20.750
I'll leave-

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.330
We'll leave the rest to you.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:29.160
As things stand, only the cores
and nothing else can get inside of Aulyn.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:32.540
Tempestas and the two of us
will clear the path.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:35.160
Amami and Imber, use that
opportunity to sneak in!

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:36.500
I can't!

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:39.700
Let us act like your upperclassmen
every once and a while!

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.750
We'll leave the finishing blow to you!

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:00.660
Now!

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:06.870
Imber!

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.870
We did it, Nebula!

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:22.540
Thank you, Hiems.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.410
If you're looking for Yayoi,

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:47.000
she went downstairs
with Mami a minute ago.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.330
Haruka...!

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:04.000
Are we inside of Aulyn?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:07.040
Nebula!

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:08.870
Hiems...!

00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:16.660
Imber...

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:20.200
I'm fine.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:28.080
It's amazing. The place where
I was born looks so small now!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.540
Is this by any chance

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:36.790
the place you meant when we discussed
where you were born a while back?

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:41.660
I see. So this is the entrance
to your homeland.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:46.700
You know, Imber, I'm just a little angry.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:50.750
I wasn't the first person you told that
you're going to protect Earth, remember?

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.700
I... Huh?

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:56.910
That isn't it?

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:02.450
It's a little strange, isn't it?
The iDOLs protecting Earth, I mean.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:03.790
True enough.

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:07.910
Nebula and Hiems aside,
even Imber is helping!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.040
He only had eyes for his Master.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.910
And here we took such good care of him.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:17.200
He probably wanted to protect his Master.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:23.950
Right, but I'm sure he'll
protect Earth while he's at it.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:46.120
I'm so happy. Imber, I...

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.330
Imber? What?

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:55.950
What do you mean that's
all you want? Imber?!

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:11.290
Imb...er? Huh? Imber?

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:09.500
Tempestas said...

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:11.290
"Goodbye."

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:17.450
Kienai uso ga omosugite
The lie that never vanishes is so heavy

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.580
Aren't those...?

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:21.660
Tsubasa oresou da yo
It feels as if my wings could snap

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:21.790
Hagiwara?

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:24.500
Futari nara... taerareru to omoeba
If it's the two of us...

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:25.200
Nubilum kept his promise...

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:29.950
Futari nara... taerareru to omoeba
I just have to believe we can endure it

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:29.950
Thank you!

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:35.040
Zetsubou datte taerareru
We can even withstand despair

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:41.450
Yakusoku wo mujaki ni chikatta ne?
You meant no harm when
you made that promise, right?

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:45.950
Naze ka shinjiteta
For some reason, I believed you

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:56.450
Shiranai kurayami ga anata
wo watashi wo tsutsumu
An unknown darkness embraces both me and you

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.200
That's right, Haruka.

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:58.660
The penguin that musters its courage
and dives into the ocean...

00:21:56.450 --> 00:22:02.700
Mitsukaranai deguchi; tobira wo tatake
I can't find the exit; pound on the door

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:00.160
...catches a whole bunch of food
and takes it back to its family!

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.000
What is that?!
...catches a whole bunch of food
and takes it back to its family!

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:01.870
Isn't this transmission from Japan?!
...catches a whole bunch of food
and takes it back to its family!

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:03.700
The radio interference is gone!
...catches a whole bunch of food
and takes it back to its family!

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:06.410
Shiawase no tame ni ai no tame dakara to
We say we do this for happiness or for love

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:06.040
We made it...

00:22:06.410 --> 00:22:11.410
Zankoku na tatakai wo kuri kaeshite
As we repeat this cruel battle

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:08.870
They go back home!

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:15.330
Sore de mo namida ga tomaranai
Yet even so, the tears won't stop

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:19.620
Negau kokoro wa issho
Our hopeful hearts are one

00:22:19.620 --> 00:22:21.370
Sorezore no mirai ga yobunda
Our own futures are calling to us

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:28.500
I
LOVE
YOU.
Sorezore no mirai ga yobunda
Our own futures are calling to us

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:50.950
Dummy! I know that, Imber.

00:22:56.450 --> 00:22:58.580
Come on, Haruka!

00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:00.080
What's keeping you!

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:02.620
I told you that the recording
is at 10:00 this morning!

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:04.580
I know that, but...!

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:06.950
Gyokuto
High

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.160
I'm going on ahead.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.370
Just give me a sec!

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:20.290
I'm off!
